      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Due to the design and implementation of the Spring Expression Language, literal numbers are always stored internally as positive numbers."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "For example, "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "-2"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is stored internally as a positive "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "2"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " which is then negated while evaluating the expression (by calculating the value of "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "0 - 2"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ")."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "This means that it is not possible to represent a negative literal number equal to the minimum value of that type of number in Java. For example, the minimum supported value for an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "int"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in Java is "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Integer.MIN_VALUE"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " which has a value of "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "-2147483648"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". However, if you include "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "-2147483648"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " in a SpEL expression, an exception will be thrown informing you that the value "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "2147483648"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " cannot be parsed as an "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "int"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " (because it exceeds the value of "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Integer.MAX_VALUE"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " which is "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "2147483647"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ")."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you need to use the minimum value for a particular type of number within a SpEL expression, you can either reference the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MIN_VALUE"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " constant for the respective wrapper type (such as "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Integer.MIN_VALUE"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Long.MIN_VALUE"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", etc.) or calculate the minimum value. For example, to use the minimum integer value:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "ulist",
            "id": null,
            "items": [
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "T(Integer).MIN_VALUE"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " — requires a "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "StandardEvaluationContext"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "blocks": [],
                "checkbox": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "-2^31"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  },
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": " — can be used with any type of "
                  },
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "EvaluationContext"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "style": null,
            "title": null
          }
        ],
